From: Lee Jones <lee@kernel.org>
Date: Wed Apr 29 13:40:41 2026 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] FROMGIT: nfc: llcp: Fix use-after-free in llcp_sock_release()

llcp_sock_release() unconditionally unlinks the socket from the local
sockets list.  However, if the socket is still in connecting state, it
is on the connecting list.

Fix this by checking the socket state and unlinking from the correct list.

Bug: 500030631
Fixes: b4011239a08e ("NFC: llcp: Fix non blocking sockets connections")
Signed-off-by: Lee Jones <lee@kernel.org>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260429134115.3558604-1-lee@kernel.org
Signed-off-by: David Heidelberg <david@ixit.cz>
(cherry picked from commit 092b1746a0beaf51ca1af94c2c1a436d22e3e182) # linux-nfc
Signed-off-by: Lee Jones <joneslee@google.com>
Change-Id: If28a08d1698b63a29a08f4024378c8aeea3da108

Origin: android.googlesource.com/kernel/common be7eb82f26606f1965d7d4b053e82570ea5f48a1
Batch: B-1 (P4 stability & functional backports) - Class A, apply as-is; predicted ABI delta zero

---
diff --git a/net/nfc/llcp_sock.c b/net/nfc/llcp_sock.c
index d5344563e5..cd1fdf0bee 100644
--- a/net/nfc/llcp_sock.c
+++ b/net/nfc/llcp_sock.c
@@ -633,6 +633,8 @@ static int llcp_sock_release(struct socket *sock)
 
 	if (sock->type == SOCK_RAW)
 		nfc_llcp_sock_unlink(&local->raw_sockets, sk);
+	else if (sk->sk_state == LLCP_CONNECTING)
+		nfc_llcp_sock_unlink(&local->connecting_sockets, sk);
 	else
 		nfc_llcp_sock_unlink(&local->sockets, sk);
 
